WEBVTT

00:00:03.703 --> 00:00:06.763
This is...
...to the USS Voyager.

00:00:06.806 --> 00:00:09.240
If you are receiving
this message...

00:00:09.275 --> 00:00:11.266
please... it carefully.

00:00:11.311 --> 00:00:13.040
We have...

00:00:14.514 --> 00:00:18.143
This is Starfleet...

00:00:18.184 --> 00:00:21.381
...receiving this message...

00:00:24.691 --> 00:00:27.626
This is Starfleet Command...

00:00:30.563 --> 00:00:33.498
...this message, study...
carefully.

00:00:33.533 --> 00:00:35.433
We have...

00:00:35.468 --> 00:00:36.833
What happened?

00:00:36.870 --> 00:00:37.802
I'm not sure.

00:00:37.837 --> 00:00:39.896
The transmission just...
stopped.

00:00:39.939 --> 00:00:40.906
Locate the source.

00:00:40.940 --> 00:00:42.202
See if you can get it back.

00:00:42.242 --> 00:00:44.107
It looks like...

00:00:44.144 --> 00:00:46.840
Captain,
the transmission was sent

00:00:46.880 --> 00:00:48.780
along the same network
of alien relay stations

00:00:48.815 --> 00:00:50.976
we used to send the Doctor
to the Alpha Quadrant.

00:00:51.017 --> 00:00:53.577
Starfleet Command must be
using them just like we did.

00:00:53.620 --> 00:00:55.315
Harry, can you clear
the interference

00:00:55.355 --> 00:00:56.322
from that message?

00:00:56.356 --> 00:00:57.618
Yes, ma'am.

00:00:57.657 --> 00:00:58.624
They said they wouldn't stop

00:00:58.658 --> 00:00:59.920
until they found
a way to get us home.

00:00:59.959 --> 00:01:02.223
Nonetheless, we can't assume
they've been able

00:01:02.262 --> 00:01:03.456
to devise a plan this quickly.

00:01:03.496 --> 00:01:05.487
They're communicating with us.

00:01:05.532 --> 00:01:06.794
That's a big step.

00:01:06.833 --> 00:01:08.801
Okay, I've reprocessed
everything we received.

00:01:08.835 --> 00:01:10.598
I've cleared out
most of the interference.

00:01:10.637 --> 00:01:11.695
Here it is.

00:01:11.738 --> 00:01:15.640
This is Starfleet Command
to the USS Voyager.

00:01:15.675 --> 00:01:17.973
If you are receiving
this message,

00:01:18.011 --> 00:01:20.275
please study it carefully.

00:01:20.313 --> 00:01:21.803
We have information...

00:01:21.848 --> 00:01:24.408
That's all we got.

00:01:24.451 --> 00:01:25.850
It looks like the bulk
of the transmission

00:01:25.885 --> 00:01:27.409
is lodged in one
of the relay stations.

00:01:27.454 --> 00:01:28.716
Can you tell which one?

00:01:28.755 --> 00:01:31.656
It's about 3.8
light-years from us

00:01:31.691 --> 00:01:34.888
on a heading of 274 mark 13.

00:01:34.928 --> 00:01:36.156
Set a course, Tom.

00:01:36.196 --> 00:01:37.823
Last time we used one
of those stations,

00:01:37.864 --> 00:01:39.422
the people who built
it weren't too happy.

00:01:39.466 --> 00:01:40.433
We'll deal with that
if we have to,

00:01:40.467 --> 00:01:42.367
but I'm not going to lose
this opportunity.

00:01:42.402 --> 00:01:45.428
We're going to find out what
the rest of that message says.

00:01:47.140 --> 00:01:49.768
This is... Command
to the USS Voyager.

00:01:49.809 --> 00:01:51.106
If you are

00:01:51.144 --> 00:01:54.409
receiving this message,
please study it carefully...

00:01:54.447 --> 00:01:56.540
Who sent this message?

00:01:56.583 --> 00:01:58.676
Unknown.
It comes from across the galaxy.

00:01:58.718 --> 00:02:01.016
Locate the ship receiving it.

00:02:01.054 --> 00:02:02.783
It's on a course
to one of our modules.

00:02:02.822 --> 00:02:04.414
Intercept.

00:04:04.509 --> 00:04:06.841
Maybe they've figured out
a way to get us home.

00:04:06.878 --> 00:04:09.904
How could they get us home
from 60,000 light-years away?

00:04:09.948 --> 00:04:11.848
Who knows
what technological advances

00:04:11.883 --> 00:04:14.443
Starfleet has come up with
since we've been gone?

00:04:14.486 --> 00:04:15.510
They might have developed

00:04:15.554 --> 00:04:17.351
a whole new way
of traveling through space.

00:04:17.389 --> 00:04:19.584
Since it was technology
that brought us

00:04:19.624 --> 00:04:21.524
to the Delta Quadrant
in the first place,

00:04:21.560 --> 00:04:23.289
it's a reasonable assumption

00:04:23.328 --> 00:04:25.558
technology
could bring us back again.

00:04:25.597 --> 00:04:26.621
Starfleet found
a stable wormhole

00:04:26.665 --> 00:04:27.632
to the Gamma Quadrant.

00:04:27.666 --> 00:04:29.759
Maybe they've discovered
one that leads here.

00:04:29.801 --> 00:04:32.793
This kind of speculation can be
intriguing, but be careful

00:04:32.838 --> 00:04:35.272
about setting yourselves up
to be disappointed.

00:04:35.307 --> 00:04:38.333
I'm just happy my folks
know I'm alive.

00:04:38.377 --> 00:04:40.743
I imagine there were
quite a few celebrations

00:04:40.779 --> 00:04:42.474
when people got the news.

00:04:42.514 --> 00:04:44.982
Probably, but I can see

00:04:45.050 --> 00:04:47.518
where it might make things
more difficult for some.

00:04:47.552 --> 00:04:50.282
I'd guess a lot of people
had given up on us...

00:04:50.322 --> 00:04:52.950
done their mourning,
gone on with their lives...

00:04:52.991 --> 00:04:54.515
found some kind of resolution.

00:04:54.559 --> 00:04:56.390
Now they get word
that we're alive,

00:04:56.428 --> 00:04:59.192
but so far away that we
might as well be dead.

00:04:59.231 --> 00:05:03.861
Some people might feel that way,
but not my mom and dad.

00:05:03.902 --> 00:05:06.564
At the very least, we know
the relay stations extend

00:05:06.605 --> 00:05:08.470
almost all the way
to the Alpha Quadrant.

00:05:08.507 --> 00:05:11.601
If Starfleet has found a way to
use them to transmit messages,

00:05:11.643 --> 00:05:13.941
we'll be able to stay
in constant contact

00:05:13.979 --> 00:05:15.105
with people at home.

00:05:15.147 --> 00:05:16.512
That has to be comforting.

00:05:16.548 --> 00:05:19.210
Sure it is, but I think
it's more comforting

00:05:19.251 --> 00:05:21.776
to think that Starfleet
is going to get us home.

00:05:21.820 --> 00:05:24.152
If no one objects, that's
what I'm going to do.

00:05:28.059 --> 00:05:29.151
You were supposed to report

00:05:29.194 --> 00:05:31.253
to Sick Bay this morning
for your weekly checkup.

00:05:31.296 --> 00:05:33.423
Where have you been?

00:05:33.465 --> 00:05:34.454
Here, doing my job.

00:05:34.499 --> 00:05:36.660
And just what is
this pressing task?

00:05:36.701 --> 00:05:38.566
I'm trying to retrieve
more of the message

00:05:38.603 --> 00:05:40.594
transmitted
from Starfleet Command.

00:05:40.639 --> 00:05:42.800
Hmm. Your devotion
to duty is admirable,

00:05:42.841 --> 00:05:44.399
but you must remember
that your implants

00:05:44.443 --> 00:05:45.967
have to be monitored
regularly.

00:05:46.077 --> 00:05:47.374
I'm fine.

00:05:47.412 --> 00:05:48.606
No, you're not.

00:05:48.647 --> 00:05:51.115
I'm detecting reduced levels
of erythrocytes in your blood.

00:05:51.149 --> 00:05:52.912
How long has it been
since you regenerated?

00:05:52.951 --> 00:05:53.508
58 hours.

00:05:53.552 --> 00:05:55.144
Well, that explains it.

00:05:55.187 --> 00:05:57.280
We've discussed this before,
Seven.

00:05:57.322 --> 00:05:58.755
You must regenerate
in your alcove

00:05:58.790 --> 00:06:00.451
for at least three hours a day.

00:06:00.492 --> 00:06:02.153
I have gone
as long as 200 hours

00:06:02.194 --> 00:06:03.286
without regenerating.

00:06:03.328 --> 00:06:04.590
That was when you were a Borg.

00:06:04.629 --> 00:06:07.393
You seem to forget you're
a good deal more human now.

00:06:07.432 --> 00:06:09.730
I assure you,
I have not forgotten.

00:06:11.002 --> 00:06:11.934
Another one.

00:06:12.003 --> 00:06:13.027
I beg your pardon?

00:06:13.071 --> 00:06:15.665
I've retrieved
another word of text.

00:06:15.707 --> 00:06:16.833
That makes six.

00:06:16.875 --> 00:06:19.901
Six words in 58 hours?

00:06:19.945 --> 00:06:21.503
Wouldn't it be
more efficient just to wait

00:06:21.546 --> 00:06:23.309
until we arrive
at the relay station?

00:06:23.348 --> 00:06:26.374
This message is important
to the Captain.

00:06:26.418 --> 00:06:27.578
I'm aware of that.

00:06:27.619 --> 00:06:30.918
In fact, if it weren't
for me, this transmission

00:06:30.956 --> 00:06:32.821
wouldn't have been possible
in the first place.

00:06:32.858 --> 00:06:34.951
I was the one
who risked my matrix

00:06:35.026 --> 00:06:36.960
in order to go
to the Alpha Quadrant.

00:06:37.028 --> 00:06:39.155
If we ever get home,

00:06:39.197 --> 00:06:43.099
I expect I'll become
quite the hero.

00:06:43.134 --> 00:06:45.625
"Emergency Medical Hologram
instrumental

00:06:45.670 --> 00:06:47.729
in the return of Voyager crew."

00:06:47.772 --> 00:06:49.967
Has a nice ring to it,
don't you think?

00:06:50.041 --> 00:06:51.668
On the other hand,
it is entirely possible

00:06:51.710 --> 00:06:52.938
that your program
will be deleted

00:06:52.978 --> 00:06:54.377
and you'll be upgraded
to conform

00:06:54.412 --> 00:06:56.209
to the most recent standards.

00:06:56.248 --> 00:06:57.840
Unlikely.

00:06:57.883 --> 00:07:02.411
I've accomplished things
no EMH ever has.

00:07:02.454 --> 00:07:05.252
In fact, most likely
I'll become

00:07:05.290 --> 00:07:08.555
an object of intense
study and discussion...

00:07:08.593 --> 00:07:09.457
possibly even veneration.

00:07:10.962 --> 00:07:12.020
What's that?

00:07:12.063 --> 00:07:13.587
Report.

00:07:13.632 --> 00:07:15.395
We're encountering some kind
of gravimetric forces.

00:07:15.433 --> 00:07:16.491
Source?

00:07:18.703 --> 00:07:19.829
Looks like it's coming

00:07:19.871 --> 00:07:21.736
from the relay station
we're heading for.

00:07:21.773 --> 00:07:24.071
That station is still
two light-years away.

00:07:24.109 --> 00:07:26.441
How could it project
a gravimetric field this far?

00:07:26.478 --> 00:07:27.445
It would have to have

00:07:27.479 --> 00:07:28.946
an incredibly powerful
energy source.

00:07:28.980 --> 00:07:31.676
I've compensated
for the disturbance.

00:07:31.716 --> 00:07:33.183
We should be all right...

00:07:33.218 --> 00:07:34.207
at least until we get closer.

00:07:34.252 --> 00:07:35.913
I'm detecting a ship, Captain.

00:07:35.954 --> 00:07:38.320
800,000 kilometers
off the port bow.

00:07:38.356 --> 00:07:39.755
On screen.

00:07:39.791 --> 00:07:41.349
It's adrift.

00:07:41.393 --> 00:07:44.760
No propulsion systems,
no weapons, no life support.

00:07:44.796 --> 00:07:47.356
I'm picking up
one male humanoid aboard.

00:07:47.399 --> 00:07:48.764
He's dead.

00:07:51.202 --> 00:07:53.966
As soon as we're close enough,
beam the body to Sick Bay.

00:07:54.005 --> 00:07:56.803
I want to know how he died.

00:08:02.047 --> 00:08:03.309
What's happened to him?

00:08:03.348 --> 00:08:06.112
He appears to have suffered
a complete osteotomy.

00:08:06.151 --> 00:08:07.550
He's been gutted.

00:08:07.586 --> 00:08:09.645
Apparently, some kind of
surgical procedure was used

00:08:09.688 --> 00:08:11.417
to remove the entire skeleton,

00:08:11.456 --> 00:08:13.754
as well as the musculature,
the ligaments and tendons,

00:08:13.792 --> 00:08:15.089
and the internal organs.

00:08:15.126 --> 00:08:16.787
How long ago did this happen?

00:08:16.828 --> 00:08:17.920
It's difficult to say.

00:08:17.996 --> 00:08:20.430
Somewhere between
a week and a month.

00:08:20.465 --> 00:08:22.057
I've seen this before.

00:08:22.100 --> 00:08:24.534
The Borg encountered
a small ship of Species 5174.

00:08:24.569 --> 00:08:26.833
They were also destroyed
in this fashion.

00:08:26.871 --> 00:08:28.839
Did you ever determine
who did it and why?

00:08:28.873 --> 00:08:30.306
No, it was irrelevant.

00:08:31.376 --> 00:08:33.742
Return the body to his ship.

00:08:33.778 --> 00:08:35.473
His people may be able
to retrieve him.

00:08:35.513 --> 00:08:36.878
Very well.

00:08:36.915 --> 00:08:38.405
When we get closer
to the station,

00:08:38.450 --> 00:08:41.044
we can use the data processors
in Astrometrics

00:08:41.086 --> 00:08:42.553
to download the message.

00:08:42.587 --> 00:08:43.576
Yes, Captain.

00:08:47.225 --> 00:08:50.888
Captain's Log, Stardate 51501.4.

00:08:50.929 --> 00:08:52.624
After two days at high warp,

00:08:52.664 --> 00:08:54.291
we're close enough
to the relay station

00:08:54.332 --> 00:08:56.960
to see it on long-range
visual sensors.

00:08:57.002 --> 00:08:59.527
Not exactly what I expected.

00:08:59.571 --> 00:09:00.538
It looks ancient.

00:09:00.572 --> 00:09:02.335
Radiometric decay ratios
indicate

00:09:02.374 --> 00:09:04.899
it's at least 100,000 years old.

00:09:05.010 --> 00:09:06.602
Scan for life-forms.

00:09:06.645 --> 00:09:07.805
Negative, sir.

00:09:07.846 --> 00:09:09.404
Looks like there's nobody home.

00:09:09.447 --> 00:09:10.914
Well, that's good news.

00:09:12.017 --> 00:09:13.143
Here we go again.

00:09:13.184 --> 00:09:15.277
The gravimetric field.

00:09:15.320 --> 00:09:17.015
Commander, if my sensors

00:09:17.055 --> 00:09:18.920
are right,
that station is using

00:09:19.024 --> 00:09:21.151
a quantum singularity
as a power source.

00:09:21.192 --> 00:09:22.318
A black hole?

00:09:22.360 --> 00:09:25.158
It's a tiny one, probably
about a centimeter in diameter,

00:09:25.196 --> 00:09:28.029
but it's putting out almost
four terawatts of energy.

00:09:28.066 --> 00:09:30.534
Then someone has managed
to contain a singularity,

00:09:30.568 --> 00:09:33.537
construct a space station
around it and tap its power.

00:09:33.571 --> 00:09:35.232
That's fascinating.

00:09:35.273 --> 00:09:36.865
Can we take this ship
any closer?

00:09:36.908 --> 00:09:38.239
I wouldn't recommend it.

00:09:38.276 --> 00:09:40.369
Voyager would take a beating
from the gravimetric eddies.

00:09:40.412 --> 00:09:41.709
All right, Tom, back us off.

00:09:41.746 --> 00:09:42.713
Aye, sir.

00:09:42.747 --> 00:09:43.771
Bridge to Janeway.

00:09:43.815 --> 00:09:44.782
Go ahead.

00:09:44.816 --> 00:09:47.683
We're as close as we're
going to be able to get.

00:09:47.719 --> 00:09:49.846
Okay. We'll see if we can
download the message from here.

00:09:49.888 --> 00:09:52.288
The datastream degraded
during transmission.

00:09:52.323 --> 00:09:54.791
Elements have been
dislocated, rearranged.

00:09:54.826 --> 00:09:57.590
It's going to require some time
to decompress the message

00:09:57.629 --> 00:09:58.857
and rearrange it
in the proper sequence.

00:09:58.897 --> 00:09:59.921
Don't worry about the sequence.

00:09:59.964 --> 00:10:01.556
Get it out in bits and pieces
if you have to.

00:10:01.599 --> 00:10:02.691
We can put it together later.

00:10:02.734 --> 00:10:04.395
I've accessed a block of data.

00:10:04.436 --> 00:10:06.631
I'm downloading the text.

00:10:10.608 --> 00:10:12.576
"How much we miss you...

00:10:14.179 --> 00:10:15.976
"We talk about you often...

00:10:16.014 --> 00:10:20.246
wondering about your... day."

00:10:20.285 --> 00:10:22.617
It sounds awfully personal
from Starfleet Command.

00:10:25.390 --> 00:10:27.950
"The children have grown
so much you wouldn't..."

00:10:34.432 --> 00:10:35.831
These are letters.

00:10:37.836 --> 00:10:40.464
These are letters from home.

00:10:48.546 --> 00:10:50.480
You'll be the official
mail carrier, Neelix.

00:10:50.515 --> 00:10:51.482
We'll get you the letters

00:10:51.516 --> 00:10:52.915
as quickly as we
can download them.

00:10:52.951 --> 00:10:55.419
A task I'm happy
to perform, Captain.

00:10:55.453 --> 00:10:58.547
I can tell you, I've never
seen the crew this excited.

00:10:58.590 --> 00:11:00.148
This is as close
as they've come

00:11:00.191 --> 00:11:02.182
to their families
in almost four years.

00:11:02.227 --> 00:11:04.718
I promise to treat these
like gemstones.

00:11:04.763 --> 00:11:05.821
By the time you've
delivered them,

00:11:05.864 --> 00:11:06.853
we should have more.

00:11:08.266 --> 00:11:09.756
Captain.

00:11:09.801 --> 00:11:11.462
I've discovered something odd.

00:11:11.503 --> 00:11:13.937
There seems to be more
here than just letters.

00:11:13.972 --> 00:11:15.098
What do you mean?

00:11:15.140 --> 00:11:17.973
There's a latent datastream
buried under the message.

00:11:18.076 --> 00:11:19.202
It's heavily encrypted.

00:11:19.244 --> 00:11:20.541
Encrypted?

00:11:20.578 --> 00:11:21.738
It appears to contain

00:11:21.780 --> 00:11:24.248
a large block of text
and what may be maps.

00:11:24.282 --> 00:11:26.307
Can you retrieve any of it?

00:11:26.351 --> 00:11:27.477
Not immediately.

00:11:27.519 --> 00:11:29.111
When more of the letters
have been cleared out,

00:11:29.154 --> 00:11:31.281
I should be able to access
the coded message.

00:11:35.126 --> 00:11:40.655
Well... I might just hope
that it contains a plan

00:11:40.698 --> 00:11:43.496
for bringing us back
to the Alpha Quadrant.

00:11:45.336 --> 00:11:46.826
I'm curious, Seven.

00:11:46.871 --> 00:11:48.168
What do you think
about all this?

00:11:48.206 --> 00:11:49.833
Messages, the possibility
of getting home?

00:11:49.874 --> 00:11:53.310
It lacks any emotional
resonance for me.

00:11:53.344 --> 00:11:54.811
I've never even been to Earth.

00:11:56.281 --> 00:11:58.476
You realize
you may have family there.

00:12:00.752 --> 00:12:02.583
That had not occurred to me.

00:12:02.620 --> 00:12:05.487
You could have cousins,
grandparents...

00:12:07.325 --> 00:12:10.226
There might be more emotional
resonance than you think.

00:12:18.436 --> 00:12:20.529
I am happy to announce

00:12:20.572 --> 00:12:23.370
that I have the first
letters from home.

00:12:23.408 --> 00:12:24.602
Who are they for, Neelix?

00:12:24.642 --> 00:12:27.975
Uh, this one is addressed
to Commander Chakotay.

00:12:32.383 --> 00:12:34.146
Who's it from, Commander?

00:12:34.185 --> 00:12:36.881
An old friend...

00:12:36.921 --> 00:12:38.821
the person who recruited
me into the Maquis.

00:12:43.928 --> 00:12:45.156
Maybe I'll read this
in private.

00:12:45.196 --> 00:12:46.891
Tom, you have the Bridge.

00:12:48.266 --> 00:12:50.291
Neelix, wait a minute.

00:12:50.335 --> 00:12:52.997
Aren't there any more?

00:12:53.071 --> 00:12:54.663
No. No more
for the Bridge crew.

00:12:54.706 --> 00:12:56.765
Not yet.

00:12:56.808 --> 00:12:58.867
Be patient.

00:13:01.779 --> 00:13:03.246
Come in.

00:13:03.281 --> 00:13:05.181
Good news, Mr. Vulcan.

00:13:05.216 --> 00:13:06.774
This one's for you.

00:13:06.818 --> 00:13:07.910
Thank you, Mr. Neelix.

00:13:07.952 --> 00:13:09.317
You can put it on the desk.

00:13:14.425 --> 00:13:15.892
Was there something more?

00:13:15.927 --> 00:13:18.259
Aren't you going to read it?

00:13:18.296 --> 00:13:20.321
Of course.

00:13:20.365 --> 00:13:23.630
I-I mean, aren't you
going to read it now?

00:13:23.668 --> 00:13:25.863
I'm finishing my weekly
tactical review.

00:13:25.904 --> 00:13:27.895
When it's completed
I'll read the message.

00:13:27.939 --> 00:13:29.133
You're going to wait

00:13:29.173 --> 00:13:31.698
until you've finished
the tactical review?

00:13:31.743 --> 00:13:33.711
Do you have
any reason to believe

00:13:33.745 --> 00:13:36.646
the content of the message
will change during that time?

00:13:36.681 --> 00:13:37.875
Well, that's not the point.

00:13:37.916 --> 00:13:39.349
It's a letter from your family.

00:13:39.384 --> 00:13:41.181
Don't you want to know
what it says?

00:13:41.219 --> 00:13:43.520
I fully intend to find out
what it says.

00:13:43.653 --> 00:13:46.486
It has some important news.

00:13:47.657 --> 00:13:49.955
You mean you've read it?

00:13:49.993 --> 00:13:52.860
Well, only the first few lines.

00:13:52.896 --> 00:13:54.363
When I was seeing
who it was addressed to,

00:13:54.397 --> 00:13:57.230
I... I couldn't help it.

00:13:57.267 --> 00:13:58.928
I-I... would you like me
to read it to you?

00:14:00.236 --> 00:14:01.464
Very well.

00:14:04.741 --> 00:14:07.676
"My husband, we have
been given the news

00:14:07.710 --> 00:14:09.200
"that you are alive.

00:14:09.245 --> 00:14:10.269
"Your children and I

00:14:10.313 --> 00:14:12.508
"have asked the priests
at the Temple of Aymonk

00:14:12.549 --> 00:14:14.949
to say prayers
for your safe return."

00:14:15.018 --> 00:14:15.882
That's very sweet.

00:14:15.919 --> 00:14:16.886
Amonak.

00:14:16.920 --> 00:14:17.887
Pardon?

00:14:17.921 --> 00:14:19.479
The Temple of Amonak...

00:14:19.522 --> 00:14:21.581
one of the most sacred
on Vulcan.

00:14:21.624 --> 00:14:23.489
Amonak. Of course.

00:14:23.526 --> 00:14:25.118
"The most significant news

00:14:25.161 --> 00:14:27.288
"is the fact
that your first son, Sek,

00:14:27.330 --> 00:14:28.922
"has gone through the Pon farr.

00:14:28.965 --> 00:14:31.058
"He mated and has
become a father.

00:14:31.100 --> 00:14:33.864
"You are now the grandfather
of a healthy female

00:14:33.903 --> 00:14:36.531
who they have named T'Meni,
after your mother."

00:14:36.573 --> 00:14:38.973
You're a grandfather!

00:14:39.075 --> 00:14:40.337
Isn't that wonderful?

00:14:40.376 --> 00:14:41.968
Congratulations!

00:14:42.011 --> 00:14:43.603
What should we call you now?

00:14:43.646 --> 00:14:45.637
Grandpa? Gramps?

00:14:45.682 --> 00:14:47.707
I think Commander Tuvok
will suffice.

00:14:47.750 --> 00:14:49.445
Thank you, Mr. Neelix.

00:14:49.485 --> 00:14:51.919
I'll read the rest to myself.

00:14:51.955 --> 00:14:53.786
Just as long as you
read it right away.

00:14:53.823 --> 00:14:55.450
No procrastinating.

00:14:55.491 --> 00:14:57.686
Who knows what else
might be in that letter?

00:15:29.225 --> 00:15:31.056
Is that a letter to you,
Captain?

00:15:31.094 --> 00:15:34.427
Yes. Seven just downloaded it.

00:15:34.464 --> 00:15:36.489
I'll be in my ready room.

00:15:36.532 --> 00:15:37.863
Yes, ma'am.

00:16:35.792 --> 00:16:37.453
Have you gotten a letter yet?

00:16:37.493 --> 00:16:39.393
Don't expect one.

00:16:41.531 --> 00:16:43.499
Do you remember Sveta?

00:16:44.967 --> 00:16:46.298
Of course.

00:16:46.335 --> 00:16:48.269
I got one from her.

00:16:48.304 --> 00:16:50.397
Why would she be writing you?

00:17:00.183 --> 00:17:01.810
Chakotay, what is it?

00:17:04.687 --> 00:17:07.155
Something terrible has happened.

00:17:07.190 --> 00:17:10.057
I read that letter for an hour
before I could accept it.

00:17:10.093 --> 00:17:12.391
Now I have to tell
everyone else...

00:17:12.428 --> 00:17:14.123
and I'm not sure how to do it.

00:17:18.601 --> 00:17:20.535
It's over, B'Elanna.

00:17:20.570 --> 00:17:22.663
There are no more Maquis.

00:17:25.041 --> 00:17:25.939
What are you saying?

00:17:26.008 --> 00:17:27.236
There are thousands of us.

00:17:27.276 --> 00:17:28.766
All wiped out.

00:17:28.811 --> 00:17:30.745
It seems the Cardassians
have an ally...

00:17:30.780 --> 00:17:32.611
a species
from the Gamma Quadrant

00:17:32.648 --> 00:17:35.014
who supplied them
with ships and weapons.

00:17:36.519 --> 00:17:38.146
Atara?

00:17:39.422 --> 00:17:40.548
Roberto?

00:17:42.358 --> 00:17:44.952
Everyone except us is dead?

00:17:44.994 --> 00:17:47.155
Just about.

00:17:47.196 --> 00:17:49.960
Sveta and a few lucky ones
are in prison.

00:17:52.168 --> 00:17:53.294
No...

00:17:53.336 --> 00:17:54.200
B'Elanna...

00:17:54.237 --> 00:17:56.637
Don't!
Don't try to console me.

00:17:56.672 --> 00:17:58.572
I don't want to be comforted.

00:17:58.608 --> 00:18:01.099
Those were our friends...

00:18:01.144 --> 00:18:03.078
good people willing to put
their lives on the line

00:18:03.112 --> 00:18:04.272
for something they believed in

00:18:04.313 --> 00:18:06.042
and now you're telling
me that they are gone...

00:18:06.082 --> 00:18:07.106
that they are slaughtered.

00:18:07.150 --> 00:18:08.208
Those are the risks we all took.

00:18:08.251 --> 00:18:09.218
We knew where it could lead.

00:18:09.252 --> 00:18:11.117
It's not right and you know it.

00:18:11.154 --> 00:18:14.351
I will make someone pay,
I swear I will.

00:18:19.428 --> 00:18:21.828
If we ever get back.

00:18:38.748 --> 00:18:41.581
Tom... I heard there are

00:18:41.617 --> 00:18:43.244
at least 30 more letters
that have been downloaded.

00:18:43.286 --> 00:18:44.275
Oh, yeah?

00:18:44.320 --> 00:18:46.652
Neelix is supposed
to be on his way here now.

00:18:46.689 --> 00:18:49.351
What do you suppose
this is, anyway?

00:18:49.392 --> 00:18:51.189
What what is?

00:18:51.227 --> 00:18:52.956
This mystery dish.

00:18:52.995 --> 00:18:54.895
It tastes vaguely like chicken,

00:18:54.931 --> 00:18:57.559
but it has the consistency
of corn husks.

00:18:57.600 --> 00:18:59.124
Is that all
you can think about...

00:18:59.168 --> 00:19:00.396
what you're eating?

00:19:00.436 --> 00:19:04.167
Well, I don't like guessing
at what I put in my stomach.

00:19:04.207 --> 00:19:07.040
Tom... we're getting
letters from home.

00:19:07.076 --> 00:19:08.475
Doesn't that mean
anything to you?

00:19:08.511 --> 00:19:10.479
Not particularly.

00:19:10.513 --> 00:19:12.572
I don't believe you.

00:19:12.615 --> 00:19:14.606
You know, it's really
not that bad.

00:19:14.650 --> 00:19:16.515
Here he comes.

00:19:16.552 --> 00:19:17.644
Good news.

00:19:17.687 --> 00:19:20.952
Seven has been able
to download some more letters.

00:19:22.158 --> 00:19:24.626
This one is for Susan Nicoletti.

00:19:24.660 --> 00:19:26.628
- Is she here?
- Oh, yes.

00:19:26.662 --> 00:19:27.253
Fitzpatrick.

00:19:27.296 --> 00:19:28.228
Right here.

00:19:28.264 --> 00:19:30.061
Thank you.

00:19:32.401 --> 00:19:33.868
Ah, Kyoto.

00:19:35.404 --> 00:19:36.393
Golwat.

00:19:39.842 --> 00:19:41.605
Thank you.

00:19:41.644 --> 00:19:42.770
Ashmore.

00:19:44.447 --> 00:19:45.607
- Dorado.
- I'm here.

00:19:45.648 --> 00:19:47.411
There's not going
to be one for me.

00:19:47.450 --> 00:19:49.441
He's not done yet.
Hang on.

00:19:49.485 --> 00:19:50.474
And finally...

00:19:51.888 --> 00:19:53.014
Parsons.

00:19:56.292 --> 00:19:57.657
I'm sorry if your name

00:19:57.693 --> 00:20:01.185
hasn't come up,
but Seven is still working.

00:20:01.230 --> 00:20:04.290
Neelix, I thought you
had over 30 letters.

00:20:04.333 --> 00:20:06.358
30?
Where did you hear that?

00:20:06.402 --> 00:20:08.495
That's what was going around.

00:20:09.538 --> 00:20:12.200
Don't pay any attention
to rumors.

00:20:14.911 --> 00:20:16.242
Right.

00:20:21.050 --> 00:20:22.984
Aren't you going
to eat your lunch?

00:20:23.019 --> 00:20:24.316
I'm not hungry.

00:20:26.789 --> 00:20:29.223
You shouldn't get
your hopes up, Harry.

00:20:29.258 --> 00:20:31.590
No hopes, no disappointments.

00:20:33.763 --> 00:20:35.731
I'm not you.

00:20:41.370 --> 00:20:42.837
Come in.

00:20:44.307 --> 00:20:45.968
Captain, I'm beginning
to have trouble

00:20:46.008 --> 00:20:47.134
accessing the datastream.

00:20:47.176 --> 00:20:49.303
The longer it remains
lodged in the relay station,

00:20:49.345 --> 00:20:50.676
the more it degrades.

00:20:50.713 --> 00:20:52.146
If we could get near enough,

00:20:52.181 --> 00:20:54.672
we could try to stabilize
the containment field,

00:20:54.717 --> 00:20:57.845
but I can't risk taking
the ship in any closer.

00:20:57.887 --> 00:21:00.651
A shuttle could withstand
the gravimetric eddies

00:21:00.690 --> 00:21:01.884
more easily than Voyager.

00:21:01.924 --> 00:21:02.913
I'd like to try it.

00:21:04.226 --> 00:21:06.387
I'd want Commander Tuvok
to go with you.

00:21:06.429 --> 00:21:07.828
For what reason?

00:21:07.863 --> 00:21:10.889
It isn't my custom
to send an away team of one.

00:21:12.268 --> 00:21:13.599
As you wish.

00:21:21.377 --> 00:21:23.345
Hi.

00:21:23.379 --> 00:21:25.813
Hi. I thought Seven
was working in here.

00:21:25.848 --> 00:21:26.837
She's gone with Tuvok

00:21:26.882 --> 00:21:28.975
to shore up the station's
confinement field.

00:21:29.018 --> 00:21:30.918
I've taken over for her.

00:21:33.055 --> 00:21:34.613
Disappointed?

00:21:34.657 --> 00:21:36.352
Of course not.

00:21:36.392 --> 00:21:37.825
Would you stop that?

00:21:37.860 --> 00:21:39.794
I've told you,
there's nothing between us.

00:21:39.829 --> 00:21:41.421
I know there's nothing
between you.

00:21:41.464 --> 00:21:42.988
It's purely
a one-way attraction.

00:21:43.032 --> 00:21:44.590
Very funny.

00:21:44.633 --> 00:21:46.658
Harry, you might as well
wear a big sign

00:21:46.702 --> 00:21:47.999
that says, "I'm in love."

00:21:48.070 --> 00:21:49.435
Everyone sees it.

00:21:49.472 --> 00:21:52.737
Look, I'll admit
that for a while...

00:21:52.775 --> 00:21:54.402
Well, she's
a very attractive woman,

00:21:54.443 --> 00:21:55.671
but I've gotten over that.

00:21:55.711 --> 00:21:57.576
Okay.

00:21:57.613 --> 00:21:59.444
Fine. Believe whatever you want.

00:21:59.482 --> 00:22:02.417
If you didn't come
down here to see her,

00:22:02.451 --> 00:22:03.850
why did you?

00:22:03.886 --> 00:22:05.581
I wanted to know...

00:22:07.323 --> 00:22:09.348
if I'd gotten a letter yet.

00:22:16.799 --> 00:22:19.768
Sorry. I haven't
seen anything so far.

00:22:22.738 --> 00:22:26.374
Do you think... there's going
to be one for everybody?

00:22:26.507 --> 00:22:28.566
I'm sure
that Starfleet contacted

00:22:28.609 --> 00:22:31.635
the families and friends
of everyone on this ship.

00:22:31.679 --> 00:22:33.613
They know how important
that would be.

00:22:33.647 --> 00:22:35.114
I hope so.

00:22:35.149 --> 00:22:37.913
Harry... you'll get one.

00:22:37.952 --> 00:22:40.045
Try to be patient.

00:22:50.831 --> 00:22:52.958
Commander, am I correct
in assuming

00:22:53.000 --> 00:22:55.195
that Vulcans are
incapable of lying?

00:22:55.236 --> 00:22:57.136
We are capable of telling lies.

00:22:57.171 --> 00:23:00.902
However, I have never found it
prudent or necessary to do so.

00:23:00.941 --> 00:23:02.465
You have never lied?

00:23:02.510 --> 00:23:05.206
Only under orders
from a superior officer.

00:23:05.246 --> 00:23:07.578
Then I must ask you something.

00:23:07.615 --> 00:23:08.946
Is it the Captain's custom

00:23:08.983 --> 00:23:11.383
to send at least two people
on an away mission?

00:23:11.419 --> 00:23:13.046
It's not only her custom,

00:23:13.087 --> 00:23:15.555
it's recommended
Starfleet protocol.

00:23:15.589 --> 00:23:18.080
I see.

00:23:18.125 --> 00:23:21.288
Is there a purpose
to your question?

00:23:21.328 --> 00:23:24.957
I am wondering if the Captain
still doesn't trust me...

00:23:24.999 --> 00:23:27.399
if she feels
I require supervision.

00:23:27.435 --> 00:23:30.427
I am not certain
how the Captain regards you,

00:23:30.471 --> 00:23:32.302
but her decision
to have me accompany you

00:23:32.339 --> 00:23:33.897
on this mission
shouldn't be taken

00:23:33.941 --> 00:23:36.000
as evidence
of any particular attitude.

00:23:38.879 --> 00:23:41.973
I believe we are close enough
to emit a polaron pulse.

00:23:42.082 --> 00:23:44.949
Bring the main deflector
on line.

00:23:44.985 --> 00:23:46.543
Ready.

00:23:51.592 --> 00:23:54.959
The variance in the containment
field is now at.29.

00:23:54.995 --> 00:23:57.225
That should prevent further
degradation of the signal.

00:23:57.264 --> 00:24:00.358
Let me ask you a question,
Seven.

00:24:00.401 --> 00:24:03.199
Is the Captain's opinion
important to you?

00:24:04.705 --> 00:24:06.468
My understanding
of the hierarchy on Voyager

00:24:06.507 --> 00:24:07.667
is that the Captain's opinion

00:24:07.708 --> 00:24:09.369
is important to every
member of the crew.

00:24:11.846 --> 00:24:12.778
What's happened?

00:24:12.813 --> 00:24:14.041
We've just been scanned

00:24:14.081 --> 00:24:16.049
by a subnucleonic beam
of some kind.

00:24:16.083 --> 00:24:18.483
The navigational sensors
have been disrupted.

00:24:18.519 --> 00:24:19.952
We must get Voyager to send out

00:24:19.987 --> 00:24:21.818
a directional beacon
to guide us back.

00:24:21.856 --> 00:24:22.948
Tuvok to Voyager.

00:24:23.023 --> 00:24:24.752
Voyager, please respond.

00:24:24.792 --> 00:24:26.885
Commander, we've lost
other systems as well.

00:24:26.927 --> 00:24:29.953
We have no communications,
no warp engines...

00:24:30.030 --> 00:24:31.691
and no weapons.

00:24:31.732 --> 00:24:33.700
I suspect this was
done intentionally

00:24:33.734 --> 00:24:35.725
by the ship
that's approaching rapidly

00:24:35.769 --> 00:24:36.827
off our port stern.

00:24:51.118 --> 00:24:54.679
They're at 50,000 kilometers
and closing.

00:24:54.722 --> 00:24:56.690
Our shields
are losing integrity.

00:24:56.724 --> 00:24:59.284
I'll try to get at least
one phaser array back on line.

00:24:59.326 --> 00:25:01.089
Commander, one more hit

00:25:01.128 --> 00:25:02.561
and we'll be susceptible
to a hull breach.

00:25:02.596 --> 00:25:04.826
That ship is larger than ours.

00:25:04.865 --> 00:25:06.594
If we lure it
closer to the station,

00:25:06.634 --> 00:25:08.568
it will be far more vulnerable

00:25:08.602 --> 00:25:10.661
to the gravitational eddies
than we are.

00:25:16.110 --> 00:25:17.737
A tractor beam.

00:25:17.778 --> 00:25:18.938
We're being pulled
toward the ship.

00:25:19.046 --> 00:25:20.741
I'll try to disrupt it.

00:25:20.781 --> 00:25:22.544
Unsuccessful.

00:25:22.583 --> 00:25:24.016
Launching a distress beacon.

00:25:35.696 --> 00:25:37.220
Torres to the Bridge.

00:25:37.264 --> 00:25:38.492
Go ahead.

00:25:38.532 --> 00:25:40.659
Captain, could Lieutenant Paris
come down here?

00:25:40.701 --> 00:25:43.499
I think I've got something
he'd want to see.

00:25:43.537 --> 00:25:45.402
He's on his way.

00:25:51.412 --> 00:25:52.379
It's a letter for you.

00:25:52.413 --> 00:25:53.573
It's coming through right now.

00:25:53.614 --> 00:25:54.842
For me?

00:25:54.882 --> 00:25:56.782
It's right here.

00:25:59.086 --> 00:26:00.644
Who's it from?

00:26:00.688 --> 00:26:01.746
I can't tell yet.

00:26:01.789 --> 00:26:05.281
Maybe it's from the rehab colony

00:26:05.326 --> 00:26:07.624
telling me
I've violated probation.

00:26:07.661 --> 00:26:10.061
Why are you acting like this?

00:26:10.097 --> 00:26:12.725
I just want to know
who the letter's from, okay?

00:26:14.234 --> 00:26:15.792
We should know in a minute.

00:26:18.205 --> 00:26:19.263
I'll be on the Bridge.

00:26:19.306 --> 00:26:20.364
What, you're not going to wait?

00:26:20.407 --> 00:26:21.897
I'm on duty.

00:26:21.942 --> 00:26:23.933
Voyager is hanging in space.

00:26:23.978 --> 00:26:25.377
There's not a lot to do
at the helm.

00:26:25.412 --> 00:26:27.710
I just thought
that I should be at my post.

00:26:27.748 --> 00:26:30.080
You may be able to fool
someone else with that ploy,

00:26:30.117 --> 00:26:31.482
but you're talking to me, Tom.

00:26:33.754 --> 00:26:36.154
Just download the letter, okay?

00:26:37.191 --> 00:26:39.318
A little more has come in.

00:26:39.360 --> 00:26:41.351
It's from Starfleet.

00:26:41.395 --> 00:26:46.059
From... an Admiral Owen.

00:26:46.100 --> 00:26:47.431
Do you know him?

00:26:49.803 --> 00:26:51.896
Admiral Owen Paris.

00:26:53.474 --> 00:26:55.339
That's my father.

00:26:55.376 --> 00:26:57.606
That's wonderful.

00:26:57.645 --> 00:27:00.478
Yeah, maybe.

00:27:05.619 --> 00:27:10.215
I... I don't know
exactly why, but...

00:27:10.257 --> 00:27:14.284
the more everybody gets excited
about these letters from home,

00:27:14.328 --> 00:27:16.853
the more I don't want
any part of it.

00:27:19.500 --> 00:27:20.728
Maybe because...

00:27:23.137 --> 00:27:26.834
what I have on Voyager...

00:27:26.874 --> 00:27:29.934
is so much better than anything
I ever had back there.

00:27:31.645 --> 00:27:34.113
I just don't want the reminder.

00:27:34.148 --> 00:27:37.584
You're not the same person
you were four years ago.

00:27:37.618 --> 00:27:39.483
What makes you think he is?

00:27:41.255 --> 00:27:42.950
No. You don't know him.

00:27:43.023 --> 00:27:44.183
At least give him a chance.

00:27:44.224 --> 00:27:45.384
He's obviously reaching out.

00:27:45.426 --> 00:27:47.485
When he forms an opinion
about something,

00:27:47.528 --> 00:27:49.894
nothing can change his mind.

00:27:51.365 --> 00:27:52.354
Fine.

00:27:56.537 --> 00:27:58.971
Excuse me if I can't feel
terribly sorry for you.

00:27:59.039 --> 00:28:03.032
I learned this morning that
a lot of my friends are dead

00:28:03.077 --> 00:28:05.910
and I've gone
from being so angry

00:28:05.946 --> 00:28:08.107
that I wanted to kill someone...

00:28:08.148 --> 00:28:11.481
to crying for an hour.

00:28:11.518 --> 00:28:13.418
And now I'm just trying to...

00:28:13.454 --> 00:28:15.854
to accept it and move on.

00:28:15.889 --> 00:28:20.519
B'Elanna... that's awful.

00:28:20.561 --> 00:28:24.053
Oh, I am so sorry.

00:28:25.666 --> 00:28:27.224
And here I am
going on about something

00:28:27.267 --> 00:28:28.632
that doesn't even matter
anymore.

00:28:28.669 --> 00:28:30.660
No, no. I'm sorry.

00:28:30.704 --> 00:28:33.229
It obviously does.

00:28:33.273 --> 00:28:35.867
You care what he thinks
about you.

00:28:37.411 --> 00:28:38.537
Yeah.

00:28:42.583 --> 00:28:44.210
Yeah, I guess I still do.

00:28:48.355 --> 00:28:51.051
I'll let you know
when I get the whole letter.

00:29:00.334 --> 00:29:02.393
Come in.

00:29:02.436 --> 00:29:05.098
Looks like Tuvok and Seven
pulled it off.

00:29:05.139 --> 00:29:07.699
The containment field
has stabilized quite a bit.

00:29:07.741 --> 00:29:09.208
B'Elanna says
she's downloading the letters

00:29:09.243 --> 00:29:10.210
much more easily now.

00:29:10.244 --> 00:29:11.211
That's good news.

00:29:11.245 --> 00:29:12.405
They don't have the shuttle
on sensors yet,

00:29:12.446 --> 00:29:13.913
but they should be back soon.

00:29:14.014 --> 00:29:16.039
I've learned
a few interesting things

00:29:16.083 --> 00:29:17.846
about that relay station.

00:29:17.885 --> 00:29:20.911
It's generating as much energy

00:29:20.954 --> 00:29:23.855
every minute as a typical
star puts out in a year.

00:29:23.891 --> 00:29:24.915
What's amazing to me

00:29:24.958 --> 00:29:27.017
is that someone
100,000 years ago

00:29:27.060 --> 00:29:29.028
was harvesting
microsingularities.

00:29:29.062 --> 00:29:31.758
If nobody shows up to protest,

00:29:31.799 --> 00:29:33.266
I'd like to stay here
for a while...

00:29:33.300 --> 00:29:35.393
try to find the answers
to some of these questions.

00:29:35.435 --> 00:29:37.300
This is the kind
of archeological puzzle

00:29:37.337 --> 00:29:39.737
that's always fascinated me.

00:29:39.773 --> 00:29:40.831
Want a cup?

00:29:40.874 --> 00:29:42.535
No, thanks.

00:29:47.614 --> 00:29:49.809
You haven't mentioned
your letter.

00:29:49.850 --> 00:29:51.249
Who was it from?

00:29:52.719 --> 00:29:53.947
It was from Mark...

00:29:54.021 --> 00:29:56.512
the man I was engaged to.

00:29:56.557 --> 00:29:58.923
He told me
about the litter of puppies

00:29:58.959 --> 00:30:01.951
my dog had...
how he found homes for them,

00:30:01.995 --> 00:30:05.431
how devastated he was
when Voyager was lost...

00:30:05.465 --> 00:30:08.059
how he held out hopes
we were alive

00:30:08.101 --> 00:30:09.728
longer than most people did...

00:30:09.770 --> 00:30:13.069
until he realized that he
was clinging to a fantasy.

00:30:13.106 --> 00:30:16.735
So he began living
his life again...

00:30:16.777 --> 00:30:21.441
meeting people,
letting go of the past.

00:30:24.718 --> 00:30:25.980
About four months ago,

00:30:26.053 --> 00:30:28.419
he married a woman
who works with him.

00:30:28.455 --> 00:30:31.015
He's very happy.

00:30:33.894 --> 00:30:35.623
And how do you feel about that?

00:30:37.598 --> 00:30:39.862
Well, I knew he'd eventually
move on with his life...

00:30:42.469 --> 00:30:45.666
but there was such
a finality to that letter.

00:30:45.706 --> 00:30:47.264
Kim to the Captain.

00:30:47.307 --> 00:30:48.399
Can you come to the Bridge?

00:30:54.948 --> 00:30:55.915
What is it?

00:30:55.949 --> 00:30:57.007
We picked up

00:30:57.050 --> 00:30:59.348
an automated distress signal
from Tuvok's shuttle.

00:30:59.386 --> 00:31:01.479
Sensors show
there's no one on board.

00:32:12.558 --> 00:32:13.889
Seven.

00:32:17.729 --> 00:32:18.991
Seven of Nine.

00:32:27.239 --> 00:32:28.968
Where are we?

00:32:29.007 --> 00:32:32.340
I assume
we're on the alien ship.

00:32:34.213 --> 00:32:36.374
This is most uncomfortable.

00:32:40.752 --> 00:32:41.980
Have you seen anyone?

00:32:42.087 --> 00:32:43.554
No.

00:32:43.589 --> 00:32:45.716
If we can reach
one of those blades,

00:32:45.757 --> 00:32:48.988
perhaps we can
cut through these bindings.

00:32:53.232 --> 00:32:55.132
You were pathetic prey.

00:32:55.868 --> 00:32:57.802
Easily taken.

00:32:57.836 --> 00:32:59.861
The hunt was not satisfying.

00:33:02.641 --> 00:33:04.268
I want information.

00:33:04.309 --> 00:33:06.937
Why do you violate our property?

00:33:06.979 --> 00:33:11.211
I could snap your puny neck
with one twist.

00:33:13.919 --> 00:33:16.114
Hardly worth taking.

00:33:16.154 --> 00:33:17.121
Answer me.

00:33:17.155 --> 00:33:18.952
Why do you use our modules?

00:33:19.024 --> 00:33:20.082
We're trying to retrieve

00:33:20.125 --> 00:33:21.956
important messages
from our home.

00:33:22.060 --> 00:33:24.961
Return us to our ship
and we'll be on our way

00:33:25.063 --> 00:33:26.462
without trespassing again.

00:33:26.498 --> 00:33:28.363
I took you in a fair hunt.

00:33:28.400 --> 00:33:30.925
I claim the relics
of the chase.

00:33:42.948 --> 00:33:44.848
Are the others on your ship

00:33:44.883 --> 00:33:47.408
able to put up more
of a fight than you?

00:33:47.452 --> 00:33:49.579
You will find our Captain
a formidable opponent

00:33:49.621 --> 00:33:51.987
and our ship heavily armed.

00:33:52.024 --> 00:33:56.324
Good. Strong prey makes
for a better hunt.

00:33:56.361 --> 00:33:57.988
Release us now
and you'll be safe.

00:33:58.030 --> 00:34:01.227
Otherwise, we will destroy you.

00:34:02.467 --> 00:34:05.459
Pitiful relics.

00:34:05.504 --> 00:34:07.563
They are the first
of their kind.

00:34:07.606 --> 00:34:09.506
I will be envied.

00:34:09.541 --> 00:34:11.202
I've located their ship.

00:34:11.243 --> 00:34:13.609
It's 4,000 ketrics
from the module.

00:34:13.645 --> 00:34:15.670
We'll be there within the hour.

00:34:15.714 --> 00:34:17.909
Go to stalking mode.

00:34:19.885 --> 00:34:21.352
Why do you hesitate?

00:34:21.386 --> 00:34:23.081
The rest of the group
is on its way.

00:34:23.121 --> 00:34:25.919
I wanted to claim
this prey for myself.

00:34:25.958 --> 00:34:27.721
We may not be able
to take them alone.

00:34:27.759 --> 00:34:30.353
We need the strength
of the others.

00:34:30.395 --> 00:34:31.953
I won't share prey
with the others.

00:34:32.064 --> 00:34:35.090
These two must be
the only relics!

00:34:35.133 --> 00:34:36.691
Prepare them!

00:34:39.805 --> 00:34:40.965
Captain.

00:34:41.039 --> 00:34:42.768
It's tricky to scan
through the interference,

00:34:42.808 --> 00:34:44.776
but I think
I'm detecting a ship.

00:34:44.810 --> 00:34:46.334
What kind of ship?

00:34:46.378 --> 00:34:48.539
Let me reconfigure
the sensor array.

00:34:48.580 --> 00:34:50.673
It's Hirogen

00:34:50.716 --> 00:34:52.809
and Tuvok and Seven
are on it.

00:34:55.320 --> 00:34:56.309
Hail them.

00:34:57.656 --> 00:34:59.317
On screen.

00:34:59.358 --> 00:35:01.690
I'm Captain Janeway
of the Starship Voyager.

00:35:01.727 --> 00:35:03.922
You have two
of my crew on board.

00:35:04.029 --> 00:35:06.759
Disconnect your link
to our module

00:35:06.798 --> 00:35:08.891
and leave this space.

00:35:08.934 --> 00:35:10.333
Not without my people.

00:35:10.369 --> 00:35:12.234
They are my relics.

00:35:12.270 --> 00:35:14.636
I'm prepared to offer
you something

00:35:14.673 --> 00:35:15.901
for their safe return.

00:35:15.941 --> 00:35:17.875
Surely we can come
to an agreement.

00:35:17.909 --> 00:35:22.369
If the rest of my group arrives,
you will be taken as well.

00:35:22.414 --> 00:35:25.349
I'm giving you a chance to run.

00:35:25.384 --> 00:35:27.147
We don't run.

00:35:27.185 --> 00:35:28.948
Captain, I've got three
more ships on sensors

00:35:28.987 --> 00:35:31.182
coming toward us at high warp.

00:35:31.223 --> 00:35:32.281
Don't be foolish.

00:35:32.324 --> 00:35:34.656
Leave now and save yourselves.

00:35:34.693 --> 00:35:37.161
Give me my people
and we'll do just that.

00:35:37.195 --> 00:35:38.719
They're mine!

00:35:38.764 --> 00:35:40.755
Then get ready for a fight.

00:35:40.799 --> 00:35:42.130
Red Alert.

00:35:49.141 --> 00:35:50.802
Are they prepared?

00:35:50.842 --> 00:35:53.640
Yes.
But now is not the time for it.

00:35:53.678 --> 00:35:55.475
We should wait
until the others arrive

00:35:55.514 --> 00:35:56.538
and take the ship.

00:35:56.581 --> 00:35:58.515
I want to make the first kill.

00:35:58.550 --> 00:35:59.983
You will verify it.

00:36:00.085 --> 00:36:02.417
If there is a battle,
we must join it.

00:36:02.454 --> 00:36:04.888
The others can wage the battle.

00:36:04.923 --> 00:36:08.120
Perhaps you are more interested
in collecting relics.

00:36:08.160 --> 00:36:11.254
Perhaps your judgment
is clouded.

00:36:11.296 --> 00:36:13.264
Don't question me again.

00:36:13.298 --> 00:36:15.163
We do it now.

00:36:15.200 --> 00:36:17.634
I suggest you think carefully
about your decision.

00:36:17.669 --> 00:36:21.765
If you kill us, our Captain will
hunt you down and show no mercy.

00:36:21.807 --> 00:36:23.775
I'm not concerned.

00:36:23.809 --> 00:36:25.174
Lower the harness.

00:36:28.213 --> 00:36:31.080
A long, coiled intestine...

00:36:31.116 --> 00:36:33.141
an interesting trophy.

00:36:33.185 --> 00:36:35.710
What possible use could you
make of my intestines?

00:36:35.754 --> 00:36:38.314
Unusual relics are prized.

00:36:38.356 --> 00:36:42.952
Yours will make me envied by men
and pursued by women.

00:36:42.994 --> 00:36:45.622
You are a crude species.

00:36:45.664 --> 00:36:48.064
Only your size
makes you formidable.

00:36:49.668 --> 00:36:53.832
Your insults are as pitiful
as your efforts to escape.

00:36:56.842 --> 00:36:58.537
This one first.

00:36:58.577 --> 00:37:02.138
I want the female to witness
what will happen to her.

00:37:02.180 --> 00:37:03.272
Their bone structure

00:37:03.315 --> 00:37:05.545
makes cutting
through the back difficult.

00:37:05.584 --> 00:37:07.142
This will take time.

00:37:12.791 --> 00:37:13.553
Bridge to Torres.

00:37:13.592 --> 00:37:14.559
Torres here, Captain.

00:37:14.593 --> 00:37:15.560
How much longer?

00:37:15.594 --> 00:37:17.118
I'm getting it out
piece by piece.

00:37:17.162 --> 00:37:18.390
At least another half hour.

00:37:18.430 --> 00:37:20.227
How are you coming?

00:37:20.265 --> 00:37:22.790
That ship has some kind
of monotanium armor plating.

00:37:22.834 --> 00:37:24.426
It's scattering
the targeting beam.

00:37:24.469 --> 00:37:25.936
The other three ships
are closing.

00:37:26.037 --> 00:37:27.163
They're within
6,000 kilometers.

00:37:27.205 --> 00:37:29.605
Captain, those ships
have massive weapons.

00:37:29.641 --> 00:37:31.233
They've definitely
got us outgunned.

00:37:31.276 --> 00:37:32.470
Harry, let me see those ships

00:37:32.511 --> 00:37:33.842
in relation
to the relay station.

00:37:33.879 --> 00:37:35.107
Yes, ma'am.

00:37:35.147 --> 00:37:37.741
Maybe we can use that quantum
singularity to our advantage.

00:37:37.782 --> 00:37:38.942
How?

00:37:39.050 --> 00:37:40.779
If we can boost the effect
of the singularity...

00:37:40.819 --> 00:37:42.810
increase the gravitational pull,

00:37:42.854 --> 00:37:43.821
we might be able to stop them.

00:37:43.855 --> 00:37:46.050
The pull would increase
if we could weaken

00:37:46.091 --> 00:37:47.388
the station's containment field.

00:37:47.425 --> 00:37:48.858
An antithoron burst might do it.

00:37:48.894 --> 00:37:50.953
If we're not careful,
we might be pulled in as well.

00:37:50.996 --> 00:37:51.963
Don't worry.

00:37:51.997 --> 00:37:53.294
We're going to be ready for it.

00:37:53.331 --> 00:37:57.290
Harry, create a low-level
warp field around Voyager...

00:37:57.335 --> 00:37:58.632
sublight energy level.

00:37:58.670 --> 00:38:01.195
That should help counteract
the gravitational pull.

00:38:01.239 --> 00:38:02.228
If the field is too strong,

00:38:02.274 --> 00:38:04.299
we won't be able to beam
Tuvok and Seven aboard.

00:38:04.342 --> 00:38:05.775
Then you'll have to find
the right balance,

00:38:05.810 --> 00:38:06.868
won't you, Harry?

00:38:06.912 --> 00:38:08.004
Yes, ma'am.

00:38:08.046 --> 00:38:09.172
On my mark,

00:38:09.214 --> 00:38:12.809
direct a level-8 antithoron
burst toward the station.

00:38:12.851 --> 00:38:15.445
Have thrusters ready
for full reverse, Mr. Paris.

00:38:15.487 --> 00:38:16.681
Understood.

00:38:16.721 --> 00:38:18.848
I've established
a low-level warp field, Captain.

00:38:18.890 --> 00:38:20.118
Antithoron system is on line.

00:38:20.158 --> 00:38:21.887
I'm ready with thrusters.

00:38:21.927 --> 00:38:22.951
Do it.

00:38:27.032 --> 00:38:28.158
It's working.

00:38:28.200 --> 00:38:29.963
Try the transporter lock
again, Harry.

00:38:32.003 --> 00:38:34.096
Stabilize the ship!

00:38:36.474 --> 00:38:39.568
I can't. The gravity well
is pulling us in!

00:38:50.555 --> 00:38:53.319
That vessel is weakening
the module's containment field.

00:38:53.358 --> 00:38:54.791
Ready weapons.

00:38:54.826 --> 00:38:56.293
Signal the others to attack.

00:38:58.129 --> 00:38:59.187
Torres to the Bridge.

00:38:59.231 --> 00:39:00.198
Janeway here.

00:39:00.232 --> 00:39:01.722
The antithoron burst
collapsed the signal.

00:39:01.766 --> 00:39:04.166
I've gotten as much of the
message as I'm going to get.

00:39:04.202 --> 00:39:05.226
Acknowledged.

00:39:05.270 --> 00:39:06.237
Hail those ships.

00:39:06.271 --> 00:39:07.465
Channel open.

00:39:07.505 --> 00:39:09.166
This is Captain Janeway.

00:39:09.207 --> 00:39:12.074
Agree to retreat, and we'll
restore the containment field.

00:39:12.110 --> 00:39:13.372
Captain, they're firing!

00:39:14.946 --> 00:39:18.040
Their weapons are destabilizing
the containment field!

00:39:18.083 --> 00:39:19.914
This is Janeway.
Stop firing.

00:39:19.985 --> 00:39:22.579
You're putting yourselves
in grave dan...

00:39:22.621 --> 00:39:23.747
The field is going!

00:39:23.788 --> 00:39:25.585
The singularity
is about to be exposed!

00:39:32.631 --> 00:39:34.462
Captain, the ship
with Tuvok and Seven

00:39:34.499 --> 00:39:35.761
is still being pulled in.

00:39:35.800 --> 00:39:36.824
Get a tractor beam on it.

00:39:36.868 --> 00:39:38.460
I have Tuvok and Seven targeted,

00:39:38.503 --> 00:39:40.130
but if we try
to transport them now,

00:39:40.171 --> 00:39:41.934
the gravity well could
scatter their patterns.

00:39:42.007 --> 00:39:42.939
The tractor beam is weakening.

00:39:43.008 --> 00:39:43.940
We're going to lose them!

00:39:44.009 --> 00:39:44.941
Harry, we have to risk it.

00:39:45.010 --> 00:39:46.637
Activating the transporter.

00:39:47.812 --> 00:39:50.940
Full reverse! Increase
power to the engines!

00:39:51.049 --> 00:39:53.210
No response.

00:39:53.251 --> 00:39:54.218
Do you have them?

00:39:54.252 --> 00:39:55.276
Not yet.

00:39:55.320 --> 00:39:56.287
Their patterns are distorting.

00:39:56.321 --> 00:39:57.618
Narrow the annular
confinement beam.

00:39:57.656 --> 00:39:58.884
Tractor beam's
almost gone, Captain.

00:39:58.923 --> 00:39:59.947
We're losing this tug-of-war.

00:40:00.058 --> 00:40:02.049
Reroute all secondary power
to the tractor emitters.

00:40:02.093 --> 00:40:03.492
The tractor beam collapsed.

00:40:03.528 --> 00:40:05.257
That ship is headed
into the black hole.

00:40:05.297 --> 00:40:06.730
I'm realigning
the pattern buffer.

00:40:06.765 --> 00:40:08.323
I've got one more shot at it.

00:40:15.940 --> 00:40:18.067
I got them!
They're in Transporter Room 2.

00:40:18.109 --> 00:40:19.076
I need more power!

00:40:19.110 --> 00:40:20.270
We're being pulled in!

00:40:20.312 --> 00:40:22.837
Transfer all available power
to the engines.

00:40:24.015 --> 00:40:25.073
It's not enough!

00:40:25.116 --> 00:40:26.413
Shut down life support.

00:40:26.451 --> 00:40:27.748
Structural integrity is failing.

00:40:27.786 --> 00:40:28.775
The hull is starting to buckle.

00:40:28.820 --> 00:40:29.809
We're going in!

00:40:29.854 --> 00:40:32.687
Open the antimatter injectors
to 120 percent.

00:40:32.724 --> 00:40:33.986
Captain, that could
breach the core.

00:40:34.059 --> 00:40:35.754
So will that black hole.
Now, just do it.

00:40:35.794 --> 00:40:36.852
Yes, ma'am.

00:40:41.866 --> 00:40:42.958
We're free.

00:40:43.001 --> 00:40:44.866
Resume course.

00:40:44.903 --> 00:40:46.962
I'll be in Astrometrics.

00:40:50.075 --> 00:40:51.474
Captain, look at this.

00:40:51.509 --> 00:40:53.636
The energy released
from the singularity

00:40:53.678 --> 00:40:56.340
created a massive discharge
along the relay network.

00:40:56.381 --> 00:40:58.474
It disabled every one
of the stations.

00:40:58.516 --> 00:41:00.484
How much of the message
were you able to get?

00:41:00.518 --> 00:41:02.611
I got most
of the encrypted Starfleet text

00:41:02.654 --> 00:41:04.246
and a few more personal letters.

00:41:04.289 --> 00:41:06.382
How soon can we see
what Starfleet had to say?

00:41:06.424 --> 00:41:07.857
Oh, it'll take
some time to decode.

00:41:07.892 --> 00:41:10.224
Harry should
probably work on it.

00:41:12.464 --> 00:41:15.763
Well, if you'll excuse me,
I have a few letters to deliver.

00:41:15.800 --> 00:41:16.789
Neelix can do that.

00:41:16.835 --> 00:41:17.961
No need.

00:41:18.002 --> 00:41:20.596
Anyway, there's one
that I want to do personally.

00:41:28.613 --> 00:41:29.705
Good news, Harry.

00:41:29.748 --> 00:41:31.841
I got this at the last minute.

00:41:34.085 --> 00:41:35.814
It's from my folks.

00:41:35.854 --> 00:41:36.843
Thanks.

00:41:43.395 --> 00:41:44.987
I'm sorry, Tom.

00:41:45.063 --> 00:41:47.429
I wasn't able
to download yours in time.

00:41:50.168 --> 00:41:52.568
Just when I was getting eager
to read it.

00:41:52.604 --> 00:41:55.198
You could assume
that he said he loves you...

00:41:56.741 --> 00:41:58.436
and that he's proud of you.

00:42:02.380 --> 00:42:03.472
I think I will.

00:42:05.817 --> 00:42:07.876
Captain's Log, supplemental.

00:42:07.919 --> 00:42:09.546
Seven of Nine
and Commander Tuvok

00:42:09.587 --> 00:42:11.384
suffered no serious
physical damage

00:42:11.423 --> 00:42:13.687
after their encounter
on the alien ship.

00:42:13.725 --> 00:42:15.955
I've been eager to hear
Tuvok's impressions

00:42:15.994 --> 00:42:17.962
of the species
who took them hostage.

00:42:17.996 --> 00:42:19.793
I learned
very little about them,

00:42:19.831 --> 00:42:22.732
but I believe we should consider
them extremely dangerous.

00:42:22.767 --> 00:42:25.531
They seem to lack
any moral center.

00:42:25.570 --> 00:42:27.060
Do you know
why the relay network

00:42:27.105 --> 00:42:28.299
was so important to them?

00:42:28.339 --> 00:42:32.400
No. I assume they used it
for communications, as we did.

00:42:32.444 --> 00:42:34.537
Well, they won't be
using it anymore.

00:42:34.579 --> 00:42:37.343
They won't be pleased
about that, Captain.

00:42:37.382 --> 00:42:39.213
I doubt we've seen
the last of them.

00:42:40.251 --> 00:42:41.240
Come in.

00:42:44.255 --> 00:42:46.587
If you'll excuse me.

00:42:46.624 --> 00:42:47.784
Commander.

00:42:47.826 --> 00:42:51.091
Repair teams have inspected
the ship from stem to stern.

00:42:51.129 --> 00:42:54.428
Except for some maintenance
that's needed on the warp coils,

00:42:54.466 --> 00:42:55.558
everything seems fine.

00:42:55.600 --> 00:42:56.794
I suppose so.

00:42:56.835 --> 00:42:57.824
Want some coffee?

00:42:57.869 --> 00:42:59.131
Thanks.

00:42:59.170 --> 00:43:00.159
Cream and sugar?

00:43:00.205 --> 00:43:01.194
Two sugars.

00:43:01.239 --> 00:43:02.900
Oh... two sugars?

00:43:02.941 --> 00:43:04.772
You know, you drink
too much of that stuff.

00:43:04.809 --> 00:43:05.776
Really?

00:43:05.810 --> 00:43:06.777
If I'm not mistaken,

00:43:06.811 --> 00:43:07.937
that's your third cup
this morning.

00:43:08.012 --> 00:43:09.673
Fourth.
And on a day like today,

00:43:09.714 --> 00:43:11.409
it won't be my last.

00:43:11.449 --> 00:43:15.545
Coffee: The finest organic
suspension ever devised.

00:43:15.587 --> 00:43:17.054
It's gotten me
through the worst

00:43:17.088 --> 00:43:18.214
of the last three years.

00:43:18.256 --> 00:43:20.884
I beat the Borg with it.

00:43:20.925 --> 00:43:25.191
Oh, I'm sure Voyager
will be fine.

00:43:25.230 --> 00:43:28.927
But I'm worried that the crew
might be a different story.

00:43:28.967 --> 00:43:31.299
I think they were
hoping mail call

00:43:31.336 --> 00:43:33.930
would become a regular part
of their day.

00:43:33.972 --> 00:43:36.133
Neelix is putting together
an impromptu party.

00:43:36.174 --> 00:43:37.641
He thought it might
cheer them up.

00:43:37.675 --> 00:43:38.972
Good idea.
When will it be?

00:43:39.010 --> 00:43:40.204
As soon as he can
get people together.

00:43:40.245 --> 00:43:41.405
Leave it to Neelix to come up

00:43:41.446 --> 00:43:43.038
with the right idea
at the right time.

00:43:45.049 --> 00:43:46.846
How are you doing?

00:43:46.885 --> 00:43:48.352
Me? I'm fine.

00:43:48.386 --> 00:43:49.944
You'd say that if you just had

00:43:49.988 --> 00:43:52.149
your legs torn off
by a Trayken beast.

00:43:52.190 --> 00:43:54.920
Look what you've been through
in the last few days.

00:43:54.959 --> 00:43:56.790
We finally make
a connection with home

00:43:56.828 --> 00:43:58.591
and then it's
ripped away from us.

00:43:58.630 --> 00:44:00.257
We manage to make another enemy

00:44:00.298 --> 00:44:01.788
who's going to try
and hunt us down

00:44:01.833 --> 00:44:05.132
and destroy us,
and on top of that...

00:44:05.169 --> 00:44:07.069
It's all right.
You can say it.

00:44:07.105 --> 00:44:10.836
On top of all that,
I got a "Dear John" letter.

00:44:13.111 --> 00:44:15.102
It wasn't really a surprise.

00:44:15.146 --> 00:44:18.582
I guess I didn't really
expect him to wait for me

00:44:18.616 --> 00:44:20.777
considering the circumstances.

00:44:20.818 --> 00:44:23.412
But it made me realize
that I was using him

00:44:23.454 --> 00:44:25.319
as a safety net, you know...

00:44:25.356 --> 00:44:28.382
as a way to avoid becoming
involved with someone else.

00:44:28.426 --> 00:44:30.553
You don't have that safety net
anymore.

00:44:30.595 --> 00:44:32.426
That's right.

00:44:32.463 --> 00:44:35.296
But then again,
my life is far from uneventful

00:44:35.333 --> 00:44:37.198
here in the Delta Quadrant.

00:44:37.235 --> 00:44:39.260
It's not like I would
have had a chance

00:44:39.304 --> 00:44:40.703
to pursue a relationship,

00:44:40.738 --> 00:44:43.229
even if I had realized
I was alone.

00:44:43.274 --> 00:44:44.901
You're hardly alone.

00:44:44.943 --> 00:44:49.209
And to my way of thinking,
there's still plenty of time.

00:44:49.247 --> 00:44:51.681
Plenty of time.

00:44:51.716 --> 00:44:54.913
Neelix to the ready room.
The party's about to begin

00:44:54.953 --> 00:44:56.250
and there are
only two people missing.

00:44:56.287 --> 00:44:58.551
We're on our way.
